omp-web (0.5.2) jammy; urgency=medium

  * The web-session store now serializes its full read-modify-write cycle
    across processes with an O_CREAT|O_EXCL lockfile, so two gateway
    instances (prod :5010 and dev :5020, sharing ~/.omp/agent) can no
    longer erase each other's sessions during login, logout, sliding-TTL
    refresh or user deletion. Writes were already atomic per file; the
    lock closes the window where a stale read snapshot from one process
    overwrote a concurrent writer's new session. Bounded acquisition with
    stale-lock takeover; no public API change (closes #23).
  * Fleet machines can now carry fallback URLs in addition to their
    primary baseUrl, in priority order. When the gateway cannot reach a
    machine over its current endpoint at connect time (DNS failure,
    ECONNREFUSED, connect timeout, TLS failure), it transparently retries
    the next endpoint; any HTTP status from the remote (401/404/500)
    means the endpoint worked and never triggers a switch. While serving
    over a fallback, the gateway lazily re-probes the primary no more
    than once per five minutes, switches back on the first success, and
    guarantees at most one in-flight probe per machine. The machine's
    active endpoint and per-endpoint health are visible through
    GET /api/machines, so the admin UI can show "on fallback". Streaming
    responses keep working over a fallback; a body already streaming is
    never replayed (closes #37).
  * The live end-to-end verification harness for #30 and #31 —
    credential-kill mid-conversation failover, sticky model identity
    across a real compaction and an idle teardown+resume, and failover
    to the conversation's own rotated chain rather than the globally
    configured first backup — is now committed and repeatable
    (refs #30, refs #31).
  * No dependency or packaging change; `bun.lock` and the `patches/`
    set are untouched from 0.5.1.

