omp-web (0.5.1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Session titles are now generated in Simplified Chinese, targeting about
    100 Hanzi, and the GitHub issue annotation moved from a trailing suffix
    to a leading prefix so the issue number survives truncation in the
    sidebar and the Home calendar. `appendIssueAnnotationSuffix` became
    `prependIssueAnnotationPrefix`; the truncation ceiling went from 120 to
    150 characters to leave room for the longest annotation prefix
    (closes #47).
  * Documentation now describes exactly one deployment method: the R2 apt
    repository. Every `git pull` + `bun install` + `bun run build` +
    `systemctl --user restart` recipe in `docs/fleet-deployment.md`,
    `AGENTS.md` and the `omp-web-restart-service` payload was replaced with
    `apt-get update && apt-get install --only-upgrade omp-web`, together
    with the one-host-at-a-time rule, the fact that an upgrade restarts the
    unit and therefore aborts every in-browser AgentSession on that host,
    and the standing hazard that 0.3.9 must be skipped because its
    `ensure_env()` omitted `patches/`. `docs/release.md` was cut down and
    its still-valid npm-publish steps moved into the `github-release`
    skill. Topology, per-host layout, the systemd unit, env
    single-sourcing, auth, security posture, version reporting and the
    restart-service protocol were all preserved rather than deleted
    (closes #48).
  * No packaging, dependency or runtime change; `bun.lock` and the
    `patches/` set are untouched from 0.5.0.

